WEBVTT

00:00:00.609 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.766 --> 00:00:03.870
In the classic lesson, we learned:

00:00:03.989 --> 00:00:06.750
one extension on each natural lash.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.750
Today, it is volume.

00:00:09.093 --> 00:00:12.350
Volume still goes on exactly one natural lash.

00:00:12.697 --> 00:00:16.030
But instead of one extension, we attach a small fan:

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:20.670
a few very fine extensions, spreading out from one shared base.

00:00:21.008 --> 00:00:24.510
The result is a full, soft and fluffy lash line.

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:26.910
It sounds like just adding more lashes.

00:00:27.355 --> 00:00:29.310
But the hard part is in one word:

00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:30.270
light.

00:00:30.994 --> 00:00:33.684
In the trade, fans are named by the number of lashes.

00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:35.844
Two lashes is 2D,

00:00:36.274 --> 00:00:39.204
three lashes is 3D, and so on.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:42.324
The largest fan in this lesson has six lashes.

00:00:42.354 --> 00:00:43.924
That is a 6D fan.

00:00:44.594 --> 00:00:47.924
Fans with even more lashes, usually called Mega Volume.

00:00:47.954 --> 00:00:49.764
We will leave for a later lesson.

00:00:50.274 --> 00:00:51.764
And the most important thing.

00:00:51.794 --> 00:00:52.804
Remember it well.

00:00:53.154 --> 00:00:57.444
However many lashes a fan has, it goes on exactly one natural lash.

00:00:58.004 --> 00:01:01.894
Never let one fan wrap two or three natural lashes at once.

00:01:03.955 --> 00:01:06.935
So why can one natural lash carry a whole fan?

00:01:07.544 --> 00:01:10.855
Because volume extensions are much finer than classic ones.

00:01:11.282 --> 00:01:14.055
Remember the picture of the small twig in the classic lesson.

00:01:14.545 --> 00:01:17.335
What the natural lash can carry stays the same.

00:01:17.684 --> 00:01:22.135
So as the number of lashes goes up, each one must get finer and lighter.

00:01:22.644 --> 00:01:27.895
A fan of a few very fine lashes can weigh about the same as one thick classic extension.

00:01:27.991 --> 00:01:29.335
An easy rule to remember:

00:01:29.448 --> 00:01:31.335
more lashes, less thickness.

00:01:31.761 --> 00:01:34.063
For the exact thickness for each type of fan,

00:01:34.013 --> 00:01:36.215
check the guide chart from your lash brand.

00:01:36.863 --> 00:01:39.829
How many D you choose is not just the client's wish:

00:01:40.178 --> 00:01:42.069
you have to look at her natural lashes.

00:01:42.338 --> 00:01:47.189
Strong, long and thick natural lashes can carry fans with more lashes.

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:53.815
Fine, short, sparse natural lashes, or lots of baby lashes, call for fewer lashes,

00:01:53.765 --> 00:01:55.189
finer and shorter:

00:01:55.575 --> 00:01:57.509
2D or 3D is enough.

00:01:57.857 --> 00:02:00.469
Even on a single eye, each zone is different.

00:02:00.722 --> 00:02:04.800
In the inner corner, the natural lashes are usually shorter and weaker,

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.389
so the fans are lighter too.

00:02:07.024 --> 00:02:08.726
Here is something that happens a lot.

00:02:08.974 --> 00:02:13.337
The client shows you a photo of very full, very dramatic lashes,

00:02:13.287 --> 00:02:14.886
and wants exactly that.

00:02:15.143 --> 00:02:17.846
While her own natural lashes are fine and sparse.

00:02:18.348 --> 00:02:22.726
If you just do what she asks, and attach fans that are too heavy, what happens?

00:02:23.233 --> 00:02:27.616
The natural lash gets pulled and bends down, the root takes the strain,

00:02:27.566 --> 00:02:29.446
and lashes can fall out early,

00:02:29.547 --> 00:02:30.326
in patches.

00:02:30.435 --> 00:02:33.926
A few months later, her natural lashes are visibly thinner.

00:02:34.241 --> 00:02:37.446
And then, the client does not blame the heavy lashes.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:38.806
She blames the salon.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:40.804
Now the fan itself.

00:02:41.251 --> 00:02:43.524
A beautiful fan has three things.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:48.804
First, a small, closed base, almost as narrow as a single lash.

00:02:49.062 --> 00:02:52.956
Only a narrow base can wrap around the natural lash, hold firmly,

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.204
and stay clear of the lash next to it.

00:02:55.613 --> 00:02:59.644
Second, the lashes spread evenly, with the same gap between them,

00:02:59.594 --> 00:03:01.604
and none of them stuck together.

00:03:01.864 --> 00:03:05.369
Third, the fan is balanced, the same on both sides,

00:03:05.319 --> 00:03:07.604
and opened just the right amount.

00:03:08.111 --> 00:03:13.367
A fan with a wide base, a lopsided spread, or lashes stuck together is heavy,

00:03:13.317 --> 00:03:16.004
sticks easily to the next natural lash,

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.084
and makes the lash line look messy.

00:03:18.697 --> 00:03:22.098
Now there are ready made fans, often called promade:

00:03:22.527 --> 00:03:24.578
the maker has already joined the base for you.

00:03:25.085 --> 00:03:29.225
There is nothing wrong with using ready made fans, especially when you are learning,

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.978
or when the client is short on time.

00:03:31.407 --> 00:03:33.874
Just choose ones with a small, neat base,

00:03:33.824 --> 00:03:37.058
and still check each fan closely before you attach it.

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:39.938
But making fans by hand is the real skill.

00:03:40.095 --> 00:03:42.455
Because you choose the number of lashes,

00:03:42.405 --> 00:03:45.458
the spread and the length to suit each natural lash.

00:03:45.965 --> 00:03:48.898
In the practice lesson, we will practice exactly that.

00:03:49.552 --> 00:03:52.182
With volume, the glue must be even less.

00:03:52.503 --> 00:03:56.262
Touch only the base of the fan to the glue drop, a very small amount.

00:03:56.711 --> 00:04:00.742
Too much glue, and the base becomes heavy and stiff, a blob.

00:04:01.251 --> 00:04:05.462
The glue creeps up between the lashes, and sticks the fan into one clump.

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:08.262
And it easily sticks to the next natural lash.

00:04:08.683 --> 00:04:10.662
Some people think more glue holds better.

00:04:11.057 --> 00:04:11.622
It does not.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.084
Lashes last because the base of the fan wraps snugly around the natural lash,

00:04:16.034 --> 00:04:17.702
not because of a lump of glue.

00:04:18.361 --> 00:04:23.426
Stickies happen even more easily in volume than in classic, because the fan is wide,

00:04:23.376 --> 00:04:24.441
with many lashes.

00:04:24.954 --> 00:04:28.922
All it takes is for one lash of the fan to touch the natural lash next to it,

00:04:28.872 --> 00:04:30.041
and you have a sticky.

00:04:30.622 --> 00:04:32.601
The result is as in the classic lesson:

00:04:32.953 --> 00:04:37.162
the two lashes grow on different schedules, get pulled, the client feels it,

00:04:37.112 --> 00:04:39.241
and the natural lashes fall out early.

00:04:39.472 --> 00:04:42.921
So isolate cleanly, and check again after each zone.

00:04:43.576 --> 00:04:47.895
New technicians often get impatient, because a volume set takes a long time.

00:04:48.477 --> 00:04:50.615
But speed does not come from rushing.

00:04:51.119 --> 00:04:52.295
It comes from technique:

00:04:52.642 --> 00:04:57.735
holding the tweezers right, making even fans, taking the right amount of glue,

00:04:57.685 --> 00:04:59.415
and placing each fan once,

00:04:59.603 --> 00:05:01.415
with no need to take it off and redo it.

00:05:02.011 --> 00:05:06.215
Rushing means too much glue and stickies, and then more time spent fixing them.

00:05:06.555 --> 00:05:08.295
Go slowly, but get it right.

00:05:08.548 --> 00:05:11.495
After many sets, your hands will speed up on their own.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:15.093
How long the lashes last depends on three things.

00:05:15.406 --> 00:05:18.960
The first is cleansing the natural lashes thoroughly before you start,

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.212
as in the classic lesson.

00:05:20.719 --> 00:05:25.013
The second is room humidity and temperature within the range the glue maker recommends.

00:05:25.453 --> 00:05:28.693
The third is the client looking after her lashes properly at home.

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:32.398
Even so, natural lashes still shed with their life cycle,

00:05:32.348 --> 00:05:35.093
so the client needs to come back for refills,

00:05:35.221 --> 00:05:36.853
usually after two to three weeks.

00:05:37.487 --> 00:05:38.704
Two more short points.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:42.539
Tweezers must be cleaned and disinfected after every client,

00:05:42.489 --> 00:05:45.503
as in the lesson on handling tools after each client.

00:05:45.853 --> 00:05:49.264
And the glue, even its fumes, can cause allergies:

00:05:49.536 --> 00:05:53.584
for the signs and what to do, see the lesson on allergies and chemicals.

00:05:54.131 --> 00:05:56.230
Finally, be honest with the client.

00:05:56.573 --> 00:05:59.510
Volume looks its best when it suits the natural lashes.

00:05:59.994 --> 00:06:02.390
If her lashes are weak, explain gently:

00:06:02.636 --> 00:06:06.378
today we will go a little lighter, so your natural lashes stay healthy,

00:06:06.328 --> 00:06:07.990
and next time we can go fuller.

00:06:08.398 --> 00:06:10.710
When clients understand, they trust you.

00:06:10.895 --> 00:06:12.790
And when they trust you, they come back.

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.154
So you see.

00:06:14.418 --> 00:06:16.954
Volume is not hard because of the many lashes.

00:06:17.338 --> 00:06:21.312
It is hard because every fan has to stay light and neat,

00:06:21.262 --> 00:06:23.834
and sit on exactly one natural lash.

00:06:24.276 --> 00:06:26.714
Once you understand, your hands will follow.

00:06:27.221 --> 00:06:31.194
In the practice lesson, we will make fans by hand, step by step.

00:06:31.539 --> 00:06:34.074
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:34.404 --> 00:06:35.194
See you next time.
